## 🟢 Solution 5: Cache Line Padding (Prevent False Sharing)

**Problem**: Thread-local counters may share cache lines, causing ping-pong.

**Solution**: Add `alignas(64)` to per-thread data:

```cpp
// In threadpool.hpp
struct alignas(64) WorkStealingQueue {  // ← Add alignas(64)
    std::deque<std::function<void()>> q;
    std::mutex mtx;
    char padding[64 - sizeof(std::mutex) % 64];  // Explicit padding
};

// Atomics that are frequently written by different threads
