```

**Problem**: When 16 threads all try to steal work, they:
1. Call `try_lock` repeatedly (spinning)
2. The mutex cache line bounces between cores
3. VTune showed: 37.8% time in `sched_yield` (waiting for locks)

### Chase-Lev Deque: The Lock-Free Alternative

**Key insight**: Owner and thieves access DIFFERENT ends of the deque:

```
         ┌───┬───┬───┬───┬───┬───┬───┬───┐
Memory:  │ 0 │ 1 │ 2 │ 3 │ 4 │ 5 │ 6 │ 7 │
         └───┴───┴───┴───┴───┴───┴───┴───┘
           ↑                           ↑
          top                       bottom
       (thieves                    (owner
        steal here)                pushes/pops here)
```

**Owner operations** (push/pop at bottom):
- Only ONE thread (owner) modifies `bottom`
- No lock needed - just atomic increment/decrement

**Thief operations** (steal from top):
- Multiple thieves compete for `top`
- Use **Compare-And-Swap (CAS)** - atomic instruction
- If CAS fails, another thief won → retry or give up

### The actual algorithm:

```cpp
// Simplified Chase-Lev (real implementation needs memory fences)

class ChaseLevDeque {
    std::atomic<int64_t> top{0};     // Thieves read/modify this
    std::atomic<int64_t> bottom{0};  // Owner reads/modifies this
    std::atomic<Task*> buffer[SIZE]; // Circular buffer

    // OWNER: Push task (no lock, no CAS)
    void push(Task* task) {
        int64_t b = bottom.load(relaxed);
        buffer[b % SIZE].store(task, relaxed);
        atomic_thread_fence(release);  // Ensure task is visible
        bottom.store(b + 1, relaxed);  // Just increment
    }

    // OWNER: Pop task (single CAS only if queue nearly empty)
    Task* pop() {
        int64_t b = bottom.load(relaxed) - 1;
        bottom.store(b, relaxed);
        atomic_thread_fence(seq_cst);  // Memory barrier
        int64_t t = top.load(relaxed);

        if (t <= b) {
            Task* task = buffer[b % SIZE].load(relaxed);
            if (t == b) {
                // Last element! Race with thieves
                if (!top.compare_exchange_strong(t, t+1)) {
                    // Lost to thief
                    bottom.store(b + 1, relaxed);
                    return nullptr;
                }
            }
            return task;
        }
        bottom.store(b + 1, relaxed);  // Queue was empty
        return nullptr;
    }

    // THIEF: Steal task (CAS-based)
    Task* steal() {
        int64_t t = top.load(acquire);
        atomic_thread_fence(seq_cst);
        int64_t b = bottom.load(acquire);

        if (t < b) {  // Queue not empty
            Task* task = buffer[t % SIZE].load(relaxed);
            if (top.compare_exchange_strong(t, t+1)) {
                // CAS succeeded - we got the task
                return task;
            }
            // CAS failed - another thief won, try again or move on
        }
        return nullptr;
    }
};
```

**Why is this faster?**

| Operation | Mutex-based | Chase-Lev |
|-----------|-------------|-----------|
| Owner push | Lock + unlock (expensive) | Atomic store (cheap) |
| Owner pop | Lock + unlock | Atomic store, rare CAS |
| Thief steal | try_lock (often fails, spins) | Single CAS (fast fail) |
| Contention | Threads wait on mutex | Threads just retry CAS |

